// Chrome bar: a view over host capabilities, never a schema of its own.
//
// There is deliberately no `spores:chrome` package. WIT is the host/guest ABI:
// one versioned contract per capability, shared by every Spore that needs it. An
// app-shaped package would mint a new contract per app, drift on every data tweak,
// and give the bar a second identity beside its manifest.
//
// So the bar imports what it reads and the manifest stays the app declaration:
//
//   soil:surface - present the bar
//   soil:time    - wall clock (wall-clock, 1.1.0) and elapsed time
//   soil:device  - battery
//   soil:shell   - workspaces and focus (package does not exist yet)
//
// One gap this bar found, soil's to close rather than chrome's to route around:
// nothing exposes shell state. `soil:view` is a viewer target, not a workspace
// list; workspace/focus belongs in a small `soil:shell` package
// (`workspaces()`, `focus()`) that any bar, launcher or agent tool can share.
// The clock gap is closed: `soil:time@1.1.0` carries `wall-clock`.
package fungos:chrome-spore@0.1.0;

world chrome-spore {
  import soil:surface/surface@1.1.0;
  import soil:surface/theme@1.1.0;
  import soil:time/time@1.1.0;
  import soil:device/battery@0.1.0;
}
